Subject: [PATCH] media: expose shared boost-bypass rail to opt-in iris diagnostic
Base-commit: cc84cab9900ee4e7a3046b3756858e9832caee72

Expose the existing PMI8994 boost-bypass regulator to the dormant Cityman iris
diagnostic. The consumer only enables it in an explicit CSI trial selector;
this patch does not change the board voltage constraints or request a voltage.
The bounded test therefore uses the existing 3.6 V board setting.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mmo/common/camera-cityman.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mmo/common/camera-cityman.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mmo/common/camera-cityman.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mmo/common/camera-cityman.dtsi
@@ -62,5 +62,6 @@
 	cityman-iris-id {
 		compatible = "microsoft,cityman-iris-id";
+		boost-supply = <&pmi8994_boostbypass>;
 		vana-supply = <&pm8994_l17>;
 		vio-supply = <&pm8994_lvs1>;
 		core-supply = <&pm8994_s3>;
